MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=13
RERELEASE=0
DESCRIPTION=KeyQuorum refusal reports stay coarse and the recipient's audit names the cause. The receive path in server file passes the checkpoint's own result to fl_kq_report_refusal_cp_in. The signed KQER report, which is carried to the sender, keeps the coarse class through fl_kq_cp_to_result (malformed as Framing, a missing key as Untrusted, too large as Denied/resource, every signature, trust, replay, freshness, fork, threshold or permit refusal as Denied/policy), so a report is not an oracle for the sender (KeyQuorum #169). The precise cause (cause=bad-signature, cause=replayed, cause=forked and the rest) is written only to the recipient's local audit line. Local problems (the destination exists, an I/O error, no driver) are still not reported. fl_kq_report_refusal_in and the checkpoint form share one writer. test_kq_service covers every cause, checks that a replay and a bad signature sign the same code and class, and checks the unreported results. Version policy: an optional RERELEASE flag (0 or 1, after DEV_VERSION when present) marks a row that reissues an existing version on purpose: a PR stacked on another PR takes its base's DEV_VERSION in its own .ver, and a GA version may be reissued on its way to main. check_version_entries_semver_dev_unique.sh requires exactly one original (RERELEASE=0 or absent) per (MAJOR, STANDARD, RELEASE, DEV_VERSION), and RERELEASE=1 needs that original and never carries GM=1. It is temporary: when the branch carrying it merges, scripts/fold_rerelease_entries.sh appends its DESCRIPTION to the original's and deletes the re-released file from version/entries and version/locked (CI on a merged push to a feature branch, Version lock on merge on develop and main). version/locked rows carry no RERELEASE line (finalize_version_locked.sh drops it; scripts/lib/ver_locked_form.sh, which the subset check compares against), and check_version_locked_immutable.sh allows a fold, and only a fold, to change a published row. tests/test_version_scripts.sh covers each rule; CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, docs/versioning.md, replit.md, the Cursor rule and .coderabbit.yaml state it. CodeQL on PR #417: both Version lock create-pull-request steps pin peter-evans/create-pull-request to 3ffccacd46053766916f087ce41d627c0b8cf2d1 (v8.1.3) instead of the mutable @v8 tag.
